<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Per-day standard deviation of each channel. Volatility roughly doubles every day from day 5 and reaches about 20 m on day 8, the day we must predict. The y channel straight through is a ramp, not a glitch: a model fitted on the quiet early days is scored on the wild end.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Consecutive readings in the GEO file are near-exact opposites, worst cosine -0.9994. The 24 largest excursions alternate sign 24 times out of 24, odds near 1 in 8 million, and all four channels flip together. Position error and clock error come from unrelated mechanisms and cannot do that. This is an artefact of the file, not the orbit.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
