338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (Cost to run. 65 ms per window on a single CPU core. Dependencies numpy and pandas. No training step, no network, no GPU. Input is exactly the five columns supplied at evaluation. For each, output is four predictions with a 1-sigma uncertainty.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (Noise. Quadrupling the measurement noise costs a few points: 51% better than doing nothing at 0.15 m, still 35% at 1.0 m, where the noise is comparable to the whole signal. The sign artefact is a different matter. One row in ten drops the model to -288%, far worse than doing nothing. We know which failure mode matters.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (Proof by construction. A clean generated GEO signal has day 8 predicted to 0.017 m. Identical physics and noise, plus their alternating-sign pattern, and the prediction flattens to 0.743 m. Where the impact is real: precise positioning, survey, timing and aviation integrity. Not the dominant term in a phone, and we say so.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
